<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 54,614 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 54,614 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 54,614 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Friday compared to 76,462 tonnes in the same period on Thursday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Friday	June 26</p>
<p>    Export cargo		 9,945	29,408</p>
<p>    Import cargo		44,669	47,054</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, five ships sailed and seven berthed. In the next 24 hours, five are expected to sail and 10 are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	Tonnes/TEUs  Ship			Berthing</p>
<p>Palm oil		4,000	 Freja Nordic	    27/6</p>
<p>High speed diesel  28,313	 Apsheron		  27/5</p>
<p>Vegoil		 10,800	 Ceilo-De-Milano	 28/6</p>
<p>Containers		550	 Contship Harmony	28/6</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
